      "en": "This is Jim. Like 'j' in 'jam'. Some dialects say it like 'g' in 'go' (Egypt)",
      "title": "Meet Jim!",
      "ar": "ج",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Jim"
    },
    {
      "en": "A curved hook shape (like reversed C) with a dot INSIDE/BELOW the curve. Jim looks like a HOOK with a dot. Hook your knowledge with Jim!",
      "title": "How to write Jim"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Jim says “ja”.",
      "title": "Jim with fatha",
      "ar": "جَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Jim says “je”.",
      "title": "Jim with kasra",
      "ar": "جِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Jim says “jo”.",
      "title": "Jim with damma",
      "ar": "جُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
